-- Arena challenges batch 9/14: rows 201-225 (track: Microprocessors & Controllers, category: ECE)

Alias = Alias_base + (byte_offset × 32) + (bit_number × 4)','{"choices": ["It compresses 32-bit words to single bits", "Each bit in a 1 MB region is aliased to a full 32 MB region — writing 1 or 0 to an alias word atomically sets/clears the corresponding bit without read-modify-write, preventing race conditions in interrupt-driven code", "Only used for SPI peripheral access", "Reduces memory footprint of firmware"], "correct": 1}'::jsonb,'Bit-banding: each bit in the bit-band region (SRAM: 0x20000000–0x20100000 or Peripheral: 0x40000000–0x40100000) maps to a 32-bit alias word. Writing 0x00000001 to the alias atomically sets the bit. Eliminates critical section around read-modify-write.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.62) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

Overhead = (switches/s × cycles/switch) / (clock frequency)','{"choices": ["0.12%", "1.2%", "12%", "0.012%"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'Context switches per second = 1000. Cycles per switch = 200. Total cycles/second = 200,000. CPU speed = 168×10⁶ cycles/s. Overhead = 200,000 / 168,000,000 = 0.00119 = 0.12%. Very low overhead — FreeRTOS is typically < 0.1% at 1 kHz tick.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.65) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

Hours to failure = endurance / writes_per_hour','{"choices": ["10,000 hours ≈ 1.14 years", "100,000 hours", "1,000 hours", "Infinite — Flash has no write limit"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'10,000 cycles / 1 cycle per hour = 10,000 hours ≈ 1.14 years. This is why frequent Flash writes in embedded systems (data logging, configuration updates) require wear levelling or external EEPROM/FRAM with 100,000–10,000,000+ cycle endurance.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.7) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;
